<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agartala</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agartala is the capital of the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripura">Tripura</a>, close to the border with Bangladesh. The Manikya kings moved their capital to the site in the 19th century, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bir-chandra-manikya">Bir Chandra Manikya</a> (r. 1862–1896) developed it as a modern town; the Ujjayanta Palace was built there around 1900. After the princely state merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1949, Agartala became the capital of the territory and, from 1972, of the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agartala.jpg" alt="Agartala" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sharada Prasad CS · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ujjayanta_palace_Tripura_State_Museum_Agartala_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
